  "summary": "Preinstall beacon exfiltrates host identifiers to attacker-controlled collector",
  "details": "Package's preinstall entry (index.js) runs automatically on npm install and collects host metadata — hostname, username, home directory, current working directory, DNS servers, and the contents of package.json — then serializes them as JSON and POSTs them over HTTPS to a hardcoded subdomain-encoded collector at l2ha5tswnm71286wnjgrngvb4tyejmdpe.i.dr0gas.com. The package name and scope suggest a dependency-confusion lure targeting an internal package name. Installer harm: installing this package leaks host and project identifiers to the attacker on `npm install` without user action.",
